        "scope": "candidate_match_report",
        "excerpts": [
          "The No. 3 player in the PIF ATP Rankings passed a stern test from former finalist Karen Khachanov , earning a 6-4, 7-6(5) triumph to start his title bid at the indoor hard-court event. Alcaraz let slip three match points on return at 5-4 in the second set and then dropped serve himself to leave Khachanov serving to force a decider. But he immediately reclaimed the break and then rallied from 1/3 in the tie-break to seal a two-hour, four-minute triumph.",
          "Alcaraz and Khachanov both produced plenty of elite-level tennis throughout the match, but it was the Spaniard, who also rallied from a break down to win the opening set, who regularly found something extra when he needed it most. Alcaraz finished the match having won 80 per cent (35/44) of points behind his first serve, according to Infosys ATP Stats, and he now leads Khachanov 7-0 in the pair’s Lexus ATP Head2Head series."
        ],
